<div class="entry-content single-content">
	
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Good laundry room organization ideas solve a familiar problem: the laundry room is one of the hardest-working rooms in the house, and one of the easiest to let slide. Baskets pile up, bottles crowd every surface, and clean clothes end up waiting on top of the dryer for days.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The fix is to organize the room around how laundry actually moves through it. This guide shows you how to organize a laundry room with a simple five-station flow, a 6-step reset and 18 ideas you can use in any size space, including a set of small laundry room organization ideas for tight rooms and closets.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/laundry-room-01-organized.jpg" alt="How to organize a laundry room: front-loading washer and dryer under a wood counter with white cabinets and baskets on open shelves" class="wp-image-704" srcset="https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/laundry-room-01-organized.jpg 1024w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/laundry-room-01-organized-300x300.jpg 300w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/laundry-room-01-organized-150x150.jpg 150w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/laundry-room-01-organized-768x768.jpg 768w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<div class="wp-block-group dsh-summary has-background" style="border-radius:12px;border-left-color:#8FA689;border-left-width:5px;background-color:#EEF3EC;padding-top:20px;padding-right:24px;padding-bottom:20px;padding-left:24px"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-0d2d72cd wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Key Takeaways</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Quick answer:</strong> To organize a laundry room, set it up in the order laundry moves: sort, wash, dry, fold or hang, and put away. Store each supply at the station where you use it, keep machine tops clear, and add a folding surface and hanging rod.</li>


<li>Organize the room around the way laundry moves: sort, wash, dry, fold, put away.</li>



<li>Keep supplies within arm&#8217;s reach of the machines.</li>



<li>A folding surface and a hanging spot stop clean clothes from piling up.</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Time:</strong> 2–4 hours · <strong>Cost:</strong> $30–150 · <strong>Difficulty:</strong> Easy</p>
